SURVIVOR EQUIVALENCE NOTES (reported as survivors, not folded into RED)

B19 `!snapshot.ConfigPresent() || !decoded` -> `&&`.
    Equivalent on every reachable state. A successful Load returns either
    loader.go:275-279 (configuration non-nil AND configPresent true) or
    loader.go:315-320 (configuration nil AND configPresent false); the two
    operands are never independently true, so the disjunct is defence in depth
    over a single reachable condition. Not a finding.

B17 / B20, with control B22.
    Adding a brand-new member to a closed vocabulary that no case supplies is
    not observable by any finite sampling suite. The mutants that admit a value
    the suite DOES supply all die: B21 ("public") and C04 ("0.0.0"). The control
    B22 shows the identical arbitrary widening survives on a sibling vocabulary
    (directory.mode) that is not part of this task's delta, so this is the
    package-wide standard and not a regression introduced here. Killing this
    class would require deriving the vocabulary from a pinned SPEC literal and
    asserting set equality with the production list. Recorded as an observation
    for a future leaf, not as a blocking finding on this one.

